","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06507","text":"Low density makes it ideal for light-weight parts","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q06502","text":"3DXSTAT ESD PA12 is made using a specialty Nylon 12 (PA12) and CNT matrix that we chose for it’s printability, thermal properties, and chemical resistance.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06505","text":"High thermal properties, with an HDT of 150C","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06508","text":"Superior chemical resistances, especially when compared to PA6 and PA6/66 nylons","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Warping and shrinkage","items":[{"id":"Q06504","text":"Our formulation ensures very low shrinkage in the printed part resulting in excellent dimensional stability, making our ESD PA12 an excellent choice for tools, fixtures, and jigs.","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06509","text":"Excellent dimensional stability and reproducible part-to-part measurements","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q06506","text":"Very low moisture absorption yielding improved retention of mechanical properties even when exposed to humid environments","source":"R-3DXTECH-READER-20261004-1e9273d6658c","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q03814","text":"Higher extrusion temperatures yield lower surface resistance values.","source":"X-3DXSTAT-ESD-PA12-TDS-v1","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q03815","text":"Therefore, the surface resistance of a printed part can be 'tuned' to your desired level of conductivity by modifying extrusion temp up or down.","source":"X-3DXSTAT-ESD-PA12-TDS-v1","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]},{"id":"G064-03","name":"Markforged Onyx ESD","maker":"Markforged","variant":null,"diameter":null,"twins":[],"composition":"\"Onyx ESD is a static dissipative safe variant of Onyx\" and \"Onyx is a micro carbon fiber filled nylon\" (p. 2, as the sheet states it); its surface resistance is 10^5 - 10^7 Ω (p. 1). The sheet names no polyamide; Markforged's safety data sheet lists carbon (9.9 to 15 %) and carbon black (8 to 12 %) and no polymer (the owner's rulings, R239).","certifications":null,"availability":null,"claim":null,"values":[{"key":"density","id":"V015697","value":1200,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-MARKFORGED-CompositesMaterialDatasheet","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Density (g/cm3), Onyx ESD"},{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V015689","value":4.2,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-MARKFORGED-CompositesMaterialDatasheet","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["direction","moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Modulus (GPa), Onyx ESD"},{"key":"tensileStrengthXY","id":"V015690","value":52,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-MARKFORGED-CompositesMaterialDatasheet","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["direction","moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Stress at Yield (MPa), Onyx ESD"},{"key":"elongationXY","id":"V015692","value":25,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-MARKFORGED-CompositesMaterialDatasheet","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["direction","moisture","treatment"],"at":"Tensile Strain at Break (%), Onyx ESD"},{"key":"flexuralModulusXY","id":"V015694